Give each thread its own cache of root value slots.

`RootValue` takes every slot from one free list under one mutex, on
both allocation and release. huggorm roots each Python `Value`, so
eight threads walking one state's values took that mutex twice per
value. Measured on an 8^6 tree, 8 threads, 5 passes: with this
serializer and huggorm's per-value registry lookup both gone, the walk
went from 0.40 s to 0.17 s and from 2.95 s to 0.89 s of CPU
(nixidae/nixidae#1557).

Each thread now keeps up to 128 free slots and moves 64 at a time to
or from the shared list. A thread's slots go back to the shared list
when it exits; a root released after that uses the shared list.

